      "content": "a substitute for a thin wooden board made by pasting sheets of paper together; especially a board of a book so made (OED s.v. pasteboard n.) | a stiff but pliable material made by pasting three or more sheets of paper together and compressing and rolling them (OED s.v. pasteboard n. & adj); a piece of board made by pasting together sheets of paper, especially for the covering of a book (ibid. II.3)"
